.TH VANPLAY 1 "October 2026" "vantool" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vanplay \- play VistaPro .VAN animations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vanplay \-modes
.br
.B vanplay
.I FILE.VAN
.RB [ \-r
.IR FPS ]
.RB [ \-l
.IR LOOPS ]
.RB [ \-p ]
.RB [ \-s
.IR FRAME ]
.RB [ \-n
.IR COUNT ]
.RB [ \-x
.IR SCALE ]
.RB [ \-f ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR OUT.BMP ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vanplay
plays the VANIM (.VAN) animations made by VistaPro 3.20 for DOS in an SDL2 window.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-r " FPS"
Frames per second. The default is 10.
.TP
.BI \-l " LOOPS"
Play this many times. 0, the default, plays forever.
.TP
.B \-p
Start paused.
.TP
.BI \-s " FRAME"
Start at this frame.
.TP
.BI \-n " COUNT"
Exit after showing
.I COUNT
frames.
.TP
.BI \-t " WHAT"
Benchmark: show
.B \-n
frames, or all of them, as fast as possible and print the frame rate.
.I WHAT
is 0 for read and draw, 1 for read only, 2 for draw only, or 3 for read through
the read-ahead buffer (two passes).
.TP
.BI \-b " KB"
Read-ahead memory. The default is 8192. 0 streams from disk.
.TP
.B \-v
Print display and buffering details on exit.
.TP
.B \-modes
List the VistaPro video modes and exit.
.TP
.BI \-x " SCALE"
Window scale. The default fits the animation in 1280x1024.
.TP
.B \-f
Fullscreen.
.TP
.BI \-c " OUT.BMP"
On exit, save the last frame shown, as rendered.
.TP
.BI \-m " MODE"
Video mode to use. This only applies to the DOS build.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BR Esc ", " q
Quit.
.TP
.B Space
Pause or resume.
.TP
.BR Left ", " Right
Step one frame back or forward.
.TP
.BR + ", " \-
Faster or slower.
.TP
.B Home
Go to the first frame.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vantool (1)
